The vision

Build a digital entertainment and learning ecosystem where children and young people across Africa can play games, develop skills, participate in competitions, express creativity and discover opportunities.

I want to approach this as a real technology product, not just a school project or another website.

The goal is to build something that users return to daily, schools can adopt, parents can trust, and sponsors eventually want to partner with.

One important product decision: NaijaPlay should not be designed as an unrestricted social network for children. It should be an activity-first platform with safe, age-appropriate interactions.

